    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450">

                <pb facs="0523" n="421" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg421"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11/1786: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China (Johnson)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-06T18:00:00-05:00">October 6, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>338. Your 781, October 2, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="45" xml:id="d450-f1"/> last
                    paragraph. Your suggestion that the Consuls General at Mukden and Harbin be
                    authorized where necessary and appropriate to address the local authorities in
                    regard to claims of American citizens arising in Manchuria, omitting names of
                    such authorities and any Manchukuo designation in the nature of titles and
                    refraining as heretofore from addressing officials of the Manchukuo central
                    régime, has the Department’s approval.</p>
                <p>Inform Mukden and Harbin.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
